/Title (Granular keyword evaluation reveals a profound cultural divergence across both semantic cohorts. Under the performance-centric taxonomy \(World A\), both markets exhibit high-volume physical optimization, with the US led by 'Weight loss' \(4,083\) and Italy heavily driven by 'Dimagrire' \(4,197\) and 'Definizione corpo' \(4,182\). Conversely, within the inclusive framework \(World B\), the Italian market shifts radically toward non-secular, self-directed velocity, anchored by 'Yoga' \(4,878\) and 'Crescita personale' \(4,569\). This localized taxonomy layout provides the foundational architecture required to align content and service delivery with specific cross-border market expectations.)
/Dest [21 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 878 0 R
>>
endobj
